{title: 005 - All My Hope on God Is Founded}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: Joachim Neander}
{composer: Herbert Howells}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: Adoration and Praise}

Verse 1:
[C]All my [Am/C]hope on [F]God is founded;
[Am]He [C]doth [Gm]still my [Am]trust [Gm]renew.
[Am]Me [F]through [Dm]change [Am]and chance [Gm]He [Edim]guideth,
[Gm]Only [Dm]good [C]and [Am]only true.
[Bb]God [Am]unknown, [F]He alone
[Gm]Calls my heart to [F]be His own.

Verse 2:
[C]Pride of [Am/C]man and [F]earthly glory,
[Am]Sword [C]and [Gm]crown betray his [F]trust;
[Am]What [F]with [Dm]care [Am]and toil [Gm]he [Edim]buildeth,
[Gm]Tower [C/E]and temple [Am]fall [C]to [Am]dust.
[Bb]But [Am]God's [Gm]power, [F]hour by [Gm]hour,
[Gm]Is my temple [F]and my tower.

Verse 3:
[C]God's great [Am/C]goodness [F]aye endureth,
[Am]Deep [C]His [Gm]wisdom, [Am]passing [F]thought;
[Am]Splendor, [Dm]light [Am]and life [Gm]attend [F]Him,
[Gm]Beauty [Dm]springeth [Am]out [Dm]of [Am]naught.
[Bb]Love [Am]doth [Gm]stand [F]at His [Gm]hand;
[Gm]Joy doth wait on [F]His command.

Verse 4:
[C]Still from [Am/C]man to [F]God eternal,
[Am]Sacrifice [Gm]of [Am]praise [Gm]be [F]done.
[Am]High [F]above [Am]all praises [Edim]praising,
[Gm]For [C]the [Dm]gift [C]of [Am]Christ [Dm]His [Am]Son.
[Bb]Christ [Am]doth [Gm]call [F]one and [Gm]all:
[Gm]Ye who follow [F]shall not fall.
